; The headless front end. This is the one place in the repo allowed to depend on
; `core_unix`: it has C stubs and does not compile to JavaScript, which is
; exactly why `lib/symbaroum` must never see it.
;
; Its own package, and that is the whole reason it has one. `dune build -p
; symbaroum` is the CI step that proves the core carries no JavaScript-hostile
; dependency, and dune builds every stanza belonging to the named package -- so
; leaving this executable in `symbaroum` would have kept the command green while
; quietly making it prove nothing. Measured, not assumed: it did.

(executable
 (name symbaroum_cli)
 (public_name symbaroum)
 (package symbaroum_cli)
 (libraries core core_unix.command_unix core_unix.filename_unix symbaroum)
 (preprocess
  (pps ppx_jane)))
